Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,The meta problem in robotics is to be able to solve a humanoid robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.68,0:00:06.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you can solve this, it'll build the biggest business in the world by a large factor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.27,0:00:08.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll own over half the world's GDP as human labor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.12,0:00:13.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,You recently went viral for comments on your OpenAI partnership with Finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.53,0:00:14.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,What happened there?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.72,0:00:18.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, OpenAI led our series B a couple years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.19,0:00:19.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,They brought in Satya and Microsoft.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.90,0:00:24.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,It got to the point where our team internally that was designing these models were running circles around OpenAI.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.09,0:00:26.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were just way better at this, so I fired them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.09,0:00:27.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I self-funded the whole company up front.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.68,0:00:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we got to a million a month of burn in 4 months.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.80,0:00:32.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Getting the robots to do the things we showed you today has almost killed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.64,0:00:35.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had record production in March, and we're going to try to 3x that by May.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.69,0:00:37.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want to be able to get to a million units a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.60,0:00:43.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've raised nearly $2 billion publicly stated at $39 billion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.82,0:00:48.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you see capital as a risk or a constraint or the valuation as a risk?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.52,0:00:51.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll just build like enormous of tens of trillions of revenue.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.87,0:00:53.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll build something massive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.14,0:00:54.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, what do most companies trade at?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.55,0:00:56.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tech companies trade at 10 or 20 times revenue.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.14,0:01:00.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're in like $10 trillion or, you know, whatever, $100 billion to $20 million in revs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.54,0:01:00.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.75,0:01:04.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is going to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.90,0:01:13.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,be a huge business.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.48,0:01:15.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Brett, welcome to Sourcery.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.40,0:01:16.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks for having me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.48,0:01:20.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know if this is going to be part one or part two, but this is a series now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.20,0:01:21.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.34,0:01:22.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.68,0:01:27.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did the entire tour, and now we're going to do a sit-down interview.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.06,0:01:32.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I figured uh we recently went viral for a lot of these hot takes at Hill and Valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.52,0:01:35.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I think it would be great if we just start there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.68,0:01:37.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what is your hottest take right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.84,0:01:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,On in robotics?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.20,0:01:41.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.56,0:01:43.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,My hot take.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.96,0:01:50.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think one thing that we spend a lot of time on is doing things with like fully autonomous and end-to-end.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.32,0:01:55.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you asked us a few questions uh here when we walked in of like, "Is this like teleoperated?"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.36,0:01:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're not teleoperating this stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.32,0:02:01.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think our hot take for robotics is just it's like it's kind of really difficult
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.17,0:02:06.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,to see what's really happening in the space without coming on site and really seeing stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.14,0:02:10.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I hope I I hope you had a good experience here today seeing everything we're doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.16,0:02:18.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think my and I think the hottest take I have is like we just want humanoid robots to work and like they're working now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.36,0:02:19.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's pretty simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.29,0:02:25.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we're seeing robots um to do everyday things like we saw it clean up a living room, do commercial work.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.25,0:02:26.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it's just it's cool to see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.49,0:02:30.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it's cool to see that this going to happen next few years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.32,0:02:37.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a very hotly contested space and it's becoming more and more competitive as It was funny
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.58,0:02:44.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,cuz we did this interview with Skydio and he was talking about Adam was talking about the drone cycles.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.27,0:02:47.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are drone cycles where there's hype cycles and that kind of thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.69,0:02:54.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,But humanoid robots are certainly at a different scale and pace than before.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.49,0:02:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, how does this feel with the competition?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.16,0:03:08.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think like the Listen, our internal goal is like how do we get these things to do real stuff and get paid for it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.00,0:03:13.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um so, we got we think a lot about how do we do autonomous useful work?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.56,0:03:14.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's our bar.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.72,0:03:19.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um we need to do that with like AI models really well and we need to do it on good good hardware.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.53,0:03:23.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like, you know, cost-effective, we can make a lot of it, we make a lot of robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.89,0:03:30.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, we think probably at this point a few years ahead of every big everybody globally doing this at this level,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.94,0:03:35.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is like um we're kind of early in the humanoid, you know, book.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.96,0:03:39.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um hopefully the next step is like how do we get more robots out at scale?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.04,0:03:42.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I we want to be first to be able to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.22,0:03:48.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we get, you know, hundreds and thousands and tens of thousands of robots in the world that run every day?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.36,0:03:49.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the the space is just early.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.03,0:03:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a lot of uh we're just like we're like in the first chapter of humanoids coming into society at scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.57,0:04:00.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um yeah, I mean we're we're we're we're pumped about here internally as it's working.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.20,0:04:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's just chapter one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.12,0:04:05.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Chapter two is like get more out the door and get them working even like uh bigger scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.69,0:04:09.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at some point we want to really be able to generalize to do everything a human can.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.20,0:04:12.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,How much do you want to produce a year?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.48,0:04:13.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's the goal?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.28,0:04:21.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we'll make thousands of robots over the like here like basically as fast as we can this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.60,0:04:25.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we're ramping bot queue like lines up as fast as we can.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.62,0:04:29.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had record production in March and we're going to 3x that by May.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.96,0:04:32.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh we'll build thousands of robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.00,0:04:38.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we basically have we already have the parts in house to do this and we're ramping up production.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.08,0:04:41.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you know, from there we want to build tens of thousands and hundreds of thousands.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.60,0:04:44.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we are you know, we want to be able to get to a million units a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.62,0:04:47.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we need the commercial progress to also to match that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.75,0:04:54.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have like so much commercial demand it's like it's hard to it we have like just overwhelmingly amount of we could I think I
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.77,0:05:02.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,could like put uh you know so I could put uh so so many robots into commercial customers today if they were were all ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.06,0:05:07.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the big gap is here is like getting the robots ready to do uh scale autonomous operations.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.16,0:05:16.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the bottleneck right now for commercializing them is it's having enough of them and making them run to a level of human performance at scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.20,0:05:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what what we don't want to do is like we don't want to put like
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.96,0:05:22.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,a thousand robots out the market and have like a thousand problems every single like hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.56,0:05:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.88,0:05:24.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's like that's not good for any of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.51,0:05:29.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we had a small batch of robots that went out to BMW last year and did work every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.92,0:05:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We ran for six months every single day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.16,0:05:32.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was phenomenal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.66,0:05:34.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,We learned we learned a ton.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.28,0:05:39.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we refactored our whole approach to how to commercialize the software and AI systems after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.48,0:05:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that kind of led us to Helix 2 which is our like second generation uh AI model internally that we like we launched a couple months ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.84,0:05:50.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,and um uh now it's like uh uh you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.77,0:05:55.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do we like put these robots into many different customers that we'll we'll probably announce a lot of this
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.34,0:06:01.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the next like 90 days and put them out into those groups uh at like decent scale like this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.43,0:06:05.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And assuming that goes well, we'll just keep we'll just keep compounding that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.20,0:06:09.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so we, you know, we had robots there last year, that went well, we learned a lot,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.48,0:06:13.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,we'll have like a much larger amount of robots going into many different customers this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.01,0:06:17.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then six to nine months goes well, we'll just we'll keep like scaling like crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.24,0:06:19.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you worried about Optimus?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.60,0:06:21.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,In my mind, this is not a manufacturing problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.50,0:06:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an intelligence problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.72,0:06:26.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're almost four years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.58,0:06:28.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,How did you scale up this fast?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.20,0:06:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,What was the process like?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.08,0:06:35.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um yeah, I've been building companies for like about 20 years now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.23,0:06:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh scaled a software company up pretty fast, sold it, scaled Archer up pretty fast, took it public.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.64,0:06:48.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so um you know, every time you know, I'm scale I'm doing I'm in this phase,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.25,0:06:53.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get to I get to sit back and say like how do what did I learn from the past experiences and how do I do it better?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.08,0:07:00.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um you know, I figure we took a a very differentiated approach to basically vertically design everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.20,0:07:07.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I don't think there's any group in the world that I wouldn't think on the robotics side that makes it designs more parts than we do on the robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.87,0:07:12.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We design the motors, basically every part within there, the rotor, stator, everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.76,0:07:21.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the sensors, the structure, the kinematics, the joints, uh we do like this, you know, the batteries that you saw today, the battery packs.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.78,0:07:24.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,That that I think has really enabled us to like control our destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.54,0:07:26.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We get to like build our own supply chain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.88,0:07:32.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh without that, you're like left at the mercy of like some vendor and then if that has an issue, like what how are you going to go solve it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.81,0:07:34.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it's got a code problem, do you understand it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.57,0:07:35.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you QA it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.21,0:07:35.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you fix it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.93,0:07:36.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you patch it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.91,0:07:40.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so we understand the whole stack from top to bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.92,0:07:43.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was an enormous lift up front to get the right people here that could do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.93,0:07:46.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we've now been iterating through as you can see behind us to
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.49,0:07:51.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,point where we like have like decently reliable systems now that run really well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.85,0:07:55.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but you know head on I self-funded the whole company up front.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.43,0:07:57.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got to you know got to a million a month of burn in four months.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.87,0:07:58.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was like a no joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.73,0:08:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had like a 40-person team in four or five months.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.12,0:08:02.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,They were like very good.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.62,0:08:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um and then just here you know 100 hours a week just trying to make it work with the team.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.52,0:08:11.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um we you know we made a we've made some mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.10,0:08:12.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've learned a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.80,0:08:15.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We done some things well and just recursively getting better.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.60,0:08:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why did you leave Archer?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.76,0:08:20.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,The the meta problem in robotics is be able to solve a humanoid robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.98,0:08:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's if you can solve this it'll build the biggest business in the world by like a large factor.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.96,0:08:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Half the world's GDP like a little under half the world's GDP is human labor.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.24,0:08:33.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I wanted to go work on building this like this holy grail of robotics.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.48,0:08:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um at Archer I you know I led design for every aircraft we have there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.72,0:08:47.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and I feel um I feel like this is now the decade we're going to bring humanoid robots to the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.40,0:08:53.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the the probably the most important maybe one of the most important businesses of our lifetime.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.08,0:08:58.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um so while I'm like a you know uh yeah so I basically get I get to I get to spend time I get
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.94,0:09:04.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,to you know get to work now on like what I think is probably the one of the more important areas of my whole career.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.36,0:09:07.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um at Archer I built the you know I built the whole team up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.72,0:09:13.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Built like uh all the led all engineering design for all the aircraft and led the company through public offering like uh so
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.73,0:09:20.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,we we're we were in a good we're now in a good spot to certify the aircraft in in inner like federal airspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.08,0:09:25.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh and Figure is also in a good spot here to really scale up like physical intelligence the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.56,0:09:31.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,I recently had Michelle Dell Buono from a16z perennial on.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.35,0:09:34.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's Mark and Ben's multi-family office.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.51,0:09:42.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we were talking through liquidity events and what you do as a founder for your first liquidity event or second or third.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.54,0:09:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why did you decide after the IPO to start another company?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.84,0:09:47.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.16,0:09:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And fund it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.08,0:09:49.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.36,0:09:53.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I started a few other companies actually since then as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.60,0:10:01.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think the short story is I feel that I've been watching the humanoid space for like a couple decades.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.08,0:10:03.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like these we've been like seeing humanoids for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.37,0:10:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've just been like the wrong we're on the wrong vector.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.04,0:10:11.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we were building the wrong stuff or we're doing it in a hobbyist grade or you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.39,0:10:14.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,um the engineering decisions were like I think we're not maybe correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.49,0:10:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I just I felt there was a need to uh advance the space much more rapidly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.88,0:10:21.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm doing the same with Harkin Cover.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.39,0:10:26.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have a couple other companies I'm doing where I also feel it's a similar situation there where I feel like
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.17,0:10:32.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,if uh left to the the world to go do it I'm unclear if like we would head to the right direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.56,0:10:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think for humanoids like, you know, the best we had 4 years ago was like a you know, Boston Dynamics had a hydraulic humanoid called Atlas.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.20,0:10:41.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It like dripped oils everywhere, lasted like 20 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.60,0:10:43.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was like very big, it very unsafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.42,0:10:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could never put it next to humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.72,0:10:48.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh classical controls methodology there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.80,0:10:54.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it was just like, man, you need to like it's like a and you know, Boston Dynamics is really a large heritage around research.
